{
  "passages": [
    {
      "block_id": "P1-S06-p01",
      "doc_id": "P1",
      "snapshot": "published",
      "heading": "Rule 5: Record All Intermediate Results, When Possible in Standardized Formats",
      "sentence_index": [
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0001",
          "text": "In principle, as long as the full process used to produce a given result is tracked, all intermediate data can also be regenerated. "
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0002",
          "text": "In practice, having easily accessible intermediate results may be of great value. "
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0003",
          "text": "Quickly browsing through intermediate results can reveal discrepancies toward what is assumed, and can in this way uncover bugs or faulty interpretations that are not apparent in the final results. "
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0004",
          "text": "Secondly, it more directly reveals consequences of alternative programs and parameter choices at individual steps. "
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0005",
          "text": "Thirdly, when the full process is not readily executable, it allows parts of the process to be rerun. "
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0006",
          "text": "Fourthly, when reproducing results, it allows any experienced inconsistencies to be tracked to the steps where the problems arise. "
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0007",
          "text": "Fifth, it allows critical examination of the full process behind a result, without the need to have all executables operational. "
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0008",
          "text": "When possible, store such intermediate results in standardized formats. "
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0009",
          "text": "As a minimum, archive any intermediate result files that are produced when running an analysis (as long as the required storage space is not prohibitive)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P2-S03-p02",
      "doc_id": "P2",
      "snapshot": "published",
      "heading": "Rule 2: Document the process, not just the results",
      "sentence_index": [
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0010",
          "text": "Many notebook users wait to add such explanatory text until the end of an analysis, after they have a solid result. "
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0011",
          "text": "Don’t wait—by that point you may have forgotten why you chose a particular parameter value, where you copied a block of code from, or what you found interesting about an intermediate result. "
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0012",
          "text": "If you do not have time to fully document what you are doing or thinking in the moment, leave short descriptive notes to remind yourself what to add when you get to a good stopping point. "
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0013",
          "text": "While the code needed to reproduce the analysis may be automatically captured in your notebook, the reasoning and intuition may not. "
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0014",
          "text": "It is okay if the story in your notebook changes over time; you should still tell a story from the very beginning, even if you don’t know the ending yet."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P2-S03-p03",
      "doc_id": "P2",
      "snapshot": "published",
      "heading": "Rule 2: Document the process, not just the results",
      "sentence_index": [
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0015",
          "text": "Clean, organize, and annotate your notebook after each experiment or meaningful chunk of work and do all your cleaning in the notebook. "
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0016",
          "text": "For example, when preparing to publish, avoid manually tweaking figures with desktop publishing tools and instead use plotting libraries with the notebook to produce publication-ready versions of figures and other artifacts to be used in manuscripts. "
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0017",
          "text": "Make sure you include your name as well as contact information for yourself and a future contact in your lab that can answer basic questions about the code. "
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0018",
          "text": "Documenting the beginning and end date of your analysis is also a good idea and can highlight the effort that you have put into the development of the notebook."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "claim": "这两篇文章报告了一项对照实验，证明给文档查证流程增加三个协作模块会使任务准确率提高20个百分点。"
}

